        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A tankless water heater can last 20 years or more, and the Department of Energy's estimate says most do. Whether yours does is decided by your water hardness, how faithfully it is descaled, and whether the vent, condensate drain and gas supply were done right. Heat exchanger warranties of 10 to 15 years are a floor, and they do not cover scale.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Test your water, fit isolation valves, descale on a schedule set by hardness, register the warranty and keep every receipt. Repair worn service parts freely, but once the heat exchanger leaks outside its warranty, put the money into a replacement.
          </p>
        </div>

